From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Let a started animation wake only the windows it changes

The threaded render loop asked every window it renders for a frame
whenever an animation started. Unless one window alone is shown, on
a vsync the loop trusts, a system timer advances animations rather
than a window's frame, so those frames advanced nothing and drew
what each window already showed: a shell of six windows drew and
presented five frames that changed nothing each time one of them
began to move. Where that timer runs, a started animation now asks
for no frames, since each item it changes asks its own window for
one, and a render-thread animator's start asks its own window to
sync (QQuickAnimatorController::requestSync). Without the timer,
where a window's frames advance the animations, it asks as before.

---
--- a/src/quick/scenegraph/qsgthreadedrenderloop.cpp
+++ b/src/quick/scenegraph/qsgthreadedrenderloop.cpp
@@ -1068,6 +1068,13 @@ void QSGThreadedRenderLoop::animationStarted()
     qCDebug(QSG_LOG_RENDERLOOP, "- animationStarted()");
     startOrStopAnimationTimer();
 
+    // With the system timer advancing animations, no window's frame does,
+    // so a frame asked of every window here draws nothing new in any of
+    // them; each item an animation changes asks its own window for one.
+    // Without the timer, a window's frame advances them, so ask as before.
+    if (m_animation_timer != 0)
+        return;
+
     for (int i=0; i<m_windows.size(); ++i)
         postUpdateRequest(const_cast<Window *>(&m_windows.at(i)));
 }
